{"turn": 5, "content": "I\u2019ll use the passing loops to separate opposing trains: T1/T2 will cross at loop 2, then T2/T3 at loop 1, while the remaining trains are held until their paths are clear.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "step_4", "index": 0, "type": "function", "function": {"name": "step", "arguments": "{\"commands\": [{\"train\": \"T1\", \"action\": \"route\", \"route\": [\"W_dep\", \"S1\", \"L1a\", \"S2\", \"L2b\", \"S3\", \"E_arr\"]}, {\"train\": \"T2\", \"action\": \"route\", \"route\": [\"E_dep\", \"S3\", \"L2a\"]}, {\"train\": \"T3\", \"action\": \"route\", \"route\": [\"W_dep\", \"S1\", \"L1a\"]}, {\"train\": \"T4\", \"action\": \"hold\"}, {\"train\": \"T5\", \"action\": \"hold\"}, {\"train\": \"T6\", \"action\": \"hold\"}], \"expected_decision_id\": 2, \"request_id\": \"r2\"}"}}]}
{"turn": 6, "content": "The first two routes are set. I\u2019m now releasing the followers into short, same-direction queues at the loops; they will wait there rather than entering a single-track section against an opposing train.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "step_5", "index": 0, "type": "function", "function": {"name": "step", "arguments": "{\"commands\": [{\"train\": \"T4\", \"action\": \"route\", \"route\": [\"W_dep\", \"S1\", \"L1a\"]}, {\"train\": \"T5\", \"action\": \"route\", \"route\": [\"E_dep\", \"S3\", \"L2a\"]}, {\"train\": \"T6\", \"action\": \"route\", \"route\": [\"W_dep\", \"S1\", \"L1a\"]}], \"expected_decision_id\": 3, \"request_id\": \"r3\"}"}}]}
